      try {
        const res = await fetch(url, { method: 'HEAD' });
        return res.status;
      } catch {
        return null; // or throw, depending on your needs
      }
    })
  );
}
```

### Why this works

- **`Promise.all` preserves order** — it resolves to an array matching the input array's indices, even though the underlying fetches complete in arbitrary order.
- **`HEAD` requests** are cheap (no body), but some servers return `405 Method Not Allowed`, so we fall back to `GET`.
- **`AbortController`** prevents hung requests from blocking the whole batch.
- **Errors are captured per URL** rather than rejecting the entire batch, so one bad URL doesn't lose the others.

If you'd rather fail fast on the first bad URL, replace `Promise.all` with `Promise.allSettled` (to always get all results) or let errors propagate naturally.

